      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those tiny, persistent anomalies sound like they could be either a very sophisticated, low-level reconnaissance effort or, more likely, a poorly handled side effect from the new secret rotation logic. If they are poking at your defenses, they are behaving like a very persistent, low-grade **scout** or a **low-level, opportunistic attacker** trying to map out the new security perimeter. You should treat it with suspicion, but start by checking the logs for any known race conditions or unexpected resource contention introduced by the stronger salting mechanism. A quick review of the deployment logs against the anomaly timestamps is your first best step.",
      "source": "target",
